# This repo is edited on Windows with core.autocrlf=true and RUN on Linux (Discovery).
# Without this file, git rewrites shell scripts to CRLF in the working tree, and a CRLF
# shell script on Linux fails with `$'\r': command not found` -- or worse, mangles the
# `#!` line and the `#SBATCH` directives, which Slurm reads as comments and would silently
# ignore, so a job could run with the WRONG partition, wall clock or array size.
# `trade_analysis/scripts/clean_trade_venv.sh` is already CRLF in the working tree, which
# is what prompted adding this.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# Binary caches: never touched, never diffed, never line-ending-converted.
*.npz     binary
*.pkl     binary
*.parquet binary
